entry.summary:
Most Node.js developers start with Express when learning backend development. But even experienced devs often overlook key architectural decisions that impact scalability, maintainability, and security. Today, we'll walk through building a clean, modular REST API using Express.js, covering: API structure Routing Controllers Middlewares Error handling Environment configs 🧱 Project Structure Start with a clean structure: project-root/ ├── controllers/ ├── routes/ ├── middlewares/ ├── models/ ├── config/ ├── utils/ ├── app.js └── server.js This modular setup scales well for growing apps. 🧪 Step-by-Step: Create a Simple API 1. Install Express npm init -y npm install express dotenv 2. Create server.js
const app = require('./app'); const PORT = process.env.PORT || 5000;
